      "body": "## What does this PR do?\n\n`MegatronLLM.serve()` and `MegatronAsyncLLM.serve()` started the OpenAI-compatible HTTP frontend without passing the engine's KV block size or its prefix-caching coordinator policy. The frontend's `InferenceClient` needs both to hash prompts for prefix-affinity routing. A served engine with prefix caching therefore could not route requests that share a prefix to the engine that already caches it.\n\nThis PR forwards `block_size_tokens` (when prefix caching is enabled) and `prefix_caching_coordinator_policy` from the engine's context to `start_text_gen_server`.\n\n## Example failure scenario(s)\n\n**Scenario (served prefix caching without routing hints)**\n\n- An engine runs with prefix caching, 256-token KV blocks, and the `longest_prefix` coordinator policy.\n- The caller starts the HTTP frontend with `llm.serve(serve_config)`.\n- Before this fix, the frontend's client received no block size or policy, so it did not hash prompts for routing.\n- With this fix, the frontend receives block size 256 and the `longest_prefix` policy.\n\n## How was this bug discovered?\n\nThe sync and async serve tests capture the arguments passed to `start_text_gen_server` and expect `block_size_tokens=256` and `prefix_caching_coordinator_policy=\"longest_prefix\"`. On `main` neither argument is passed.\n\n## Dependency and scope\n\nThis PR is independent and based on `main`. The change is limited to the `serve()` methods in `apis/llm.py` and `apis/async_llm.py`. The regression is a new test, `test_serve_forwards_prefix_caching_routing_settings`, which covers both `MegatronLLM` and `MegatronAsyncLLM`. The existing serve tests are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nExact tested commit: `2d9e6585c219071fb7f8a77e9a0a6759996ff258`.\n\n- **H100, job 20916673, and GB200, job 8372839:** `high_level_api/test_apis.py` on 1 rank: 27 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped on each.\n- **Fix-reverted control, H100 job 20916673:** with the production change reverted, the new test failed for both classes because `start_text_gen_server` received no `block_size_tokens` argument.\n- Black, isort, Ruff and `git diff --check` pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
